  "behavior": [
    "A closed frame plan derives actual record, UTF-8, shape, sidecar and move capacities from admitted selections before the original account protects them. Fixed workers validate health around construction/mutation/finish and retain nested tensor custody through failed delivery and unwind.",
    "Ordinary capture Context includes its explicit cached opening prefix while Sequence and local predictions retain existing semantics. Zero-origin and independent-invocation identity preimages remain unchanged. Geometry, preflight, checkpoint forks and intervention evidence consume the retained origin.",
    "SharedCapturePlan moves admitted data into immutable aliasable storage, counts actual retained nested capacities and attaches existing source custody once per domain. Physical identity is separate from semantic identity and does not retain the payload or its charge.",
    "Future Full/Slice/Preview workspace tracing keeps the original workspace context and imported backing identity, checks exact source axes and prices a possible nonempty F32 cast despite precision-erased metadata. Actual execution and future quotation share one selection program."
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "Root reviewed production changes and all new tests. Independent exact-source reviews covered shared plan capacities/custody and ordinary origin propagation; their frozen source hashes are preserved.",
    "A frame partial-unwind test expected ExecutionFenced from an unrelated unquoted acquisition. Existing pool semantics correctly return ReservedWorkActive while the quarantined reservation remains live. Only that expected error changed; original failed runtime log and one-line patch are retained.",
    "The shared-plan package was rebased additively onto the origin package: only module exports and exhaustive handling of the new inline text_origin field changed. The exact rebase and integrated source hashes are retained.",
    "The frozen origin consumer audit describes checkpoint sizing imprecisely: size_of<CaptureCheckpoint> includes its inline admitted plan; it does not directly call size_of<AdmittedCapturePlan>. The implementation was reviewed. Intervention rejection before estimator use is source-reviewed; the new test does not count estimator calls."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No managed instrumentation capability gate changed. Global scheduled host protection/one-use claims, source registration, original observer-aware quote, lazy hook publication and public ordinary/controlled delivery remain integration work.",
    "Frame construction does not itself grant invocation quota, tensor provenance or native completion. Shared plan capacity is retained-payload accounting, not a bound for discovery/admission construction peaks.",
    "Nonzero-origin intervention coupling currently returns a typed unsupported rejection. Intervention origin integration is unfinished, not an inherent model limitation.",
    "No new released-checkpoint comparison, process-memory measurement or native distributed validation. Existing allocator/control-bookkeeping boundary remains."
  ]
}
